/-!
# A perfect factor of a regular immersion

Let `i : Z ⟶ Y` and `j : Y ⟶ X` be immersions of schemes with `X` locally Noetherian, let `i`
be perfect, and suppose the composite `i ≫ j` is a regular immersion.  Then `i` is a regular
immersion, and `j` is a regular immersion on a neighbourhood of the image of `i`.  This is
Stacks tag 09RK.

The proof is the source's.  At a point `z` of `Z` the two kernels

* `I = ker (O_{X, j (i z)} ⟶ O_{Y, i z})`, and
* `J = ker (O_{X, j (i z)} ⟶ O_{Z, z})`

are nested ideals of the Noetherian local ring `A = O_{X, j (i z)}`, with `J` generated by a
regular sequence because `i ≫ j` is regular.  Perfectness of `i` says that `A ⧸ J = O_{Z, z}`
has finite projective dimension over `A ⧸ I = O_{Y, i z}`, which is the hypothesis of Stacks
tag 09PV; that tag makes the map of cotangent spaces `I/𝔪I ⟶ J/𝔪J` injective, and Stacks tag
09PW then generates both `I` and `J/I` by regular sequences.  Since `X` is locally Noetherian
the resulting conditions on local rings are equivalent to regularity of the ideal sheaves, by
Stacks tag 063I, so `i` is regular everywhere and `j` is regular at each point of `i(Z)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_of_isRegularImmersion`:
  a regular immersion generates the kernel of each of its maps of local rings by a regular
  sequence.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap`:
  the converse over a locally Noetherian target, which is the regular case of Stacks tag 063I
  read along an immersion.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isOpen_regularStalkLocus`: the set of points of the
  source at which an immersion into a locally Noetherian scheme generates the kernel of its map
  of local rings by a regular sequence is open.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isRegularImmersion_of_perfect`: **Stacks tag 09RK**
  for `i`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_opens_isRegularImmersion_comp_of_perfect`:
  **Stacks tag 09RK** for `j`, corrected (a Stacks erratum): `j` is a regular immersion on an
  open neighbourhood of the image of `i`.

## Implementation notes

**The conclusion for `j` is stated on a neighbourhood of the image of `i`, and it has to be: a
Stacks erratum.**  The source's literal conclusion is that `i` *and*
`j` are regular immersions, and that does not follow from its hypotheses.  Over a field `k`,
take `Z = Spec k`, `Y = Spec k ⊔ Spec k`, `X = Spec k ⊔ Spec k[ε]/(ε²)`, let `i` be the inclusion
of the first component of `Y`, and let `j` be the identity on the first component and the reduced
point `Spec k ↪ Spec k[ε]/(ε²)` on the second.  Then `X` is locally Noetherian, being the
spectrum of the Noetherian ring `k × k[ε]/(ε²)`, and `i` and `i ≫ j` are both the inclusion of a
component, hence open immersions, hence regular immersions, so `i` is perfect; but `j` is not a
regular immersion, because on the second component its ideal `(ε) ⊆ k[ε]/(ε²)` is generated by no
weakly regular sequence — every element of `(ε)` kills `ε ≠ 0`.  The refutation is
`Stacks.Examples.not_forall_isRegularImmersion_of_perfect_of_isRegularImmersion_comp`.  (The
degenerate `Z = ∅` already shows the conclusion is unobtainable, but says nothing about where the
failure lives; the example above does, and it satisfies the hypotheses with `Z` nonempty.)

The source's own proof is local at the points of `i(Z)` — it produces, for each `z : Z`, a
regular sequence generating the kernel of `O_{X, j (i z)} ⟶ O_{Y, i z}` — and says nothing at
points of `Y` outside the image of `i`;  in the example `i(Z)` is the first component, and the
second is exactly where `j` fails.  What those local conclusions do give is an open `V ⊆ Y`
containing `i(Z)` with `V.ι ≫ j` a regular immersion, and that is what is proved here.  The locus
where the local conclusion holds is open by `isOpen_regularStalkLocus`, so `V` may be taken to be
that locus itself rather than a union of chosen neighbourhoods.

**No gluing step is needed.** `IsRegularIdealSheaf` is by definition a condition at each point of
the support of the quotient, and the affine criterion of Stacks tag 063G keeps it in that form,
so the passage from "regular at every point" to "regular" is the criterion itself.  The spreading
out of a regular sequence from a local ring to an affine neighbourhood is the implication
`(1) ⇒ (5)` of Stacks tag 063I, which is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.exists_affineOpen_span_eq_ideal_isRegular`.

**The two bridges to the stalk are set up for an arbitrary closed immersion, not for the
canonical closed subscheme.** The kernel of the stalk map of a closed immersion `m` is the ideal
that `m.ker` cuts out in the local ring, because both are the extension of the ideal of sections
over an affine open along the germ map — `Stacks.Flatness.ker_stalkMap_eq_map_germ` for the one
and `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.stalkIdeal_eq_map_germ` for the other.  Reading this off
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_stalkMap_subschemeι` instead would require
identifying `m` with `m.ker.subschemeι` first.

**The defining ideal sheaf of a morphism is spelled
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.definingIdealOfHom`
here.** The library carries two abbreviations of that name, one in `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry` and
one in `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf`;  they have the same value, so they are
interchangeable up to definitional unfolding, but not for `rw`.  The support lemma
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.definingIdealQuotient_support_eq_range` and the generation criterion
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isGeneratedByOn_definingIdealOfHom_of_ker_app_eq_span` are stated for
the first, which is why the statements below name it explicitly even though this file lives in
the second namespace.

**Passing between an immersion and its canonical closed factor is a ring isomorphism at the
stalk.** An immersion `f` factors as `f.liftCoborder ≫ f.coborderRange.ι` with the second map an
open immersion, so its stalk maps are isomorphisms; regular generators of a kernel are carried
along a ring isomorphism precomposed with the map, which is
`exists_isRegular_ker_comp_ringEquiv_iff` below.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 37.62.11 (Tag 09RK)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09RK)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 23.9.5 (Tag 09PW)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PW)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 23.9.4 (Tag 09PV)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PV)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.6 (Tag 063I)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063I)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.2 (Tag 063G)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063G)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry RingTheory.Sequence
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

universe u

section RingTransport

/-- **Regular generators of a kernel are carried along a ring isomorphism.**  If `f : R' → R` is
an isomorphism of commutative rings, with inverse `f'`, then the kernel of `g : R → S` is
generated by a regular sequence of `R` exactly when the kernel of `g ∘ f` is generated by a
regular sequence of `R'`.

The isomorphism is presented by the two maps and the two round-trip identities rather than as a
`RingEquiv`, so that it may be applied to a stalk map of an open immersion, whose inverse is the
categorical one. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_ker_comp_ringEquiv_iff {R R' S : Type u}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing R'] [CommRing S] (f : R' →+* R) (f' : R →+* R')
    (hff' : ∀ x : R', f' (f x) = x) (hf'f : ∀ y : R, f (f' y) = y) (g : R →+* S) :
    (∃ rs : List R', IsRegular R' rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (g.comp f)) ↔
      ∃ rs : List R, IsRegular R rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker g := by
  have key : ∀ {T T' : Type u} [CommRing T] [CommRing T'] (p : T' →+* T) (p' : T →+* T'),
      (∀ x : T', p' (p x) = x) → (∀ y : T, p (p' y) = y) → ∀ (q : T →+* S),
      (∃ rs : List T, IsRegular T rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker q) →
        ∃ rs : List T', IsRegular T' rs ∧ Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (q.comp p) := by
    intro T T' _ _ p p' hpp' hp'p q h
    obtain ⟨rs, hreg, hspan⟩ := h
    let e : T ≃+ T' :=
      { toFun := p'
        invFun := p
        left_inv := hp'p
        right_inv := hpp'
        map_add' := map_add p' }
    refine ⟨rs.map p', ?_, ?_⟩
    · refine (AddEquiv.isRegular_congr (e := e) ?_).mp hreg
      refine List.forall₂_map_right_iff.mpr (List.forall₂_same.mpr ?_)
      intro a _ x
      exact map_mul p' a x
    · have hmap : Ideal.map p' (RingHom.ker q) = RingHom.ker (q.comp p) := by
        refine le_antisymm (Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun y hy => ?_) fun y hy => ?_
        · simp only [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker, RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
            hp'p]
          exact hy
        · have hy' : p y ∈ RingHom.ker q := by
            simpa only [RingHom.mem_ker, RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply] using hy
          exact hpp' y ▸ Ideal.mem_map_of_mem p' hy'
      rw [← Ideal.map_ofList, hspan, hmap]
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, key f f' hff' hf'f g⟩
  have hcomp : (g.comp f).comp f' = g := RingHom.ext fun y => by
    simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, hf'f]
  exact hcomp ▸ key f' f hf'f hff' (g.comp f) h

end RingTransport

section OpenFactor

/-- The map of local rings induced by a composite is the composite of the induced maps. -/
private theorem hom_stalkMap_comp {Z W X : Scheme.{u}} (k : Z ⟶ W) (b : W ⟶ X) (z : Z) :
    ((k ≫ b).stalkMap z).hom = (k.stalkMap z).hom.comp (b.stalkMap (k.base z)).hom := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp]; rfl

/-- **Regular generators of a stalk kernel are the same before and after an open immersion on the
target.**  For `k : Z ⟶ W` and `b : W ⟶ X` an open immersion, the kernel of the map of local
rings induced by `k ≫ b` at `z` is generated by a regular sequence exactly when the kernel of the
one induced by `k` is. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_comp_isOpenImmersion_iff {Z W X : Scheme.{u}}
    (k : Z ⟶ W) (b : W ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion b] (z : Z) :
    (∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk ((k ≫ b).base z)),
        IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk ((k ≫ b).base z)) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker ((k ≫ b).stalkMap z).hom) ↔
      ∃ rs : List (W.presheaf.stalk (k.base z)),
        IsRegular (W.presheaf.stalk (k.base z)) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (k.stalkMap z).hom := by
  rw [hom_stalkMap_comp]
  let e := asIso (b.stalkMap (k.base z))
  refine exists_isRegular_ker_comp_ringEquiv_iff (b.stalkMap (k.base z)).hom e.inv.hom
    (fun x => ?_) (fun y => ?_) (k.stalkMap z).hom
  · exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom e.hom_inv_id x
  · exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom e.inv_hom_id y

/-- **An open immersion on the source does not change the kernel of a stalk map.**  For
`a : Z' ⟶ Z` an open immersion and `f : Z ⟶ X`, the kernel of the map of local rings induced by
`a ≫ f` at `z` is the kernel of the one induced by `f` at `a z`, because the stalk map of `a` is
an isomorphism. -/
private theorem ker_stalkMap_isOpenImmersion_comp {Z' Z X : Scheme.{u}} (a : Z' ⟶ Z)
    [IsOpenImmersion a] (f : Z ⟶ X) (z : Z') :
    RingHom.ker ((a ≫ f).stalkMap z).hom = RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap (a.base z)).hom := by
  have hinj : Function.Injective (a.stalkMap z).hom :=
    (asIso (a.stalkMap z)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.injective
  rw [hom_stalkMap_comp]
  exact RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _ hinj

/-- **Regular generators of a stalk kernel of an immersion and of its canonical closed factor.**
An immersion `f` factors as the closed immersion `f.liftCoborder` followed by the open immersion
`f.coborderRange.ι`, so the kernel of its map of local rings at `z` is generated by a regular
sequence exactly when the kernel of the corresponding map for `f.liftCoborder` is. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_iff {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion f] (z : Z) :
    (∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)), IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap z).hom) ↔
      ∃ rs : List (f.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (f.liftCoborder.base z)),
        IsRegular (f.coborderRange.toScheme.presheaf.stalk (f.liftCoborder.base z)) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (f.liftCoborder.stalkMap z).hom := by
  have h := exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_comp_isOpenImmersion_iff f.liftCoborder
    f.coborderRange.ι z
  rw [f.liftCoborder_ι] at h
  exact h

end OpenFactor

section StalkKernel

/-- **The kernel of the stalk map of a closed immersion is the ideal its kernel ideal sheaf cuts
out in the local ring.**  Both are the extension, along the germ map of an affine open
neighbourhood, of the ideal of sections of the kernel ideal sheaf over that open. -/
private theorem stalkIdeal_ker_eq_ker_stalkMap {Z W : Scheme.{u}} (m : Z ⟶ W)
    [IsClosedImmersion m] (z : Z) (hz : m.base z ∈ m.ker.support) :
    stalkIdeal m.ker (m.base z) hz = RingHom.ker (m.stalkMap z).hom := by
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hzU, -⟩ := W.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
    (Set.mem_univ (m.base z)) isOpen_univ
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (m.appLE U (m ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app]
    exact m.app_surjective U hU
  have hgerm : RingHom.ker (m.stalkMap z).hom
      = (RingHom.ker (m.appLE U (m ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom).map
        (W.presheaf.germ U (m.base z) hzU).hom :=
    Stacks.Flatness.ker_stalkMap_eq_map_germ m hU (hU.preimage m) le_rfl hzU hzU hsurj
  have hideal : RingHom.ker (m.appLE U (m ⁻¹ᵁ U) le_rfl).hom = m.ker.ideal ⟨U, hU⟩ := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE_eq_app]
    exact (Scheme.Hom.ker_apply m ⟨U, hU⟩).symm
  rw [hgerm, hideal, stalkIdeal_eq_map_germ m.ker (m.base z) hz hU hzU]

/-- **An affine open carrying regular generators of the defining ideal of a closed immersion.**
If the kernel of the map of local rings of a closed immersion `m` at `z` is generated by a
regular sequence and the target is locally Noetherian, then the defining ideal sheaf of `m` is
generated over some affine open neighbourhood of `m z` by a sequence that is regular in the ring
of sections there.

This is the spreading out `(1) ⇒ (5)` of Stacks tag 063I applied to the kernel ideal sheaf of
`m`, together with the identification of its sections over an affine open with the kernel of
`m.app`. -/
private theorem exists_affineOpen_isGeneratedByOn_isRegular {Z W : Scheme.{u}} (m : Z ⟶ W)
    [IsClosedImmersion m] [IsLocallyNoetherian W] (z : Z)
    (h : ∃ rs : List (W.presheaf.stalk (m.base z)), IsRegular (W.presheaf.stalk (m.base z)) rs ∧
      Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (m.stalkMap z).hom) :
    ∃ (U : W.affineOpens) (_ : m.base z ∈ (U.1 : Set W)) (r : ℕ) (g : Fin r → Γ(W, U.1)),
      IsGeneratedByOn W.toRingedSpace
          (_root_.Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.definingIdealOfHom m) U.1 g ∧
        IsRegular Γ(W, U.1) (List.ofFn g) := by
  obtain ⟨rs, hreg, hspan⟩ := h
  have hz : m.base z ∈ m.ker.support := m.range_subset_ker_support ⟨z, rfl⟩
  have hget : List.ofFn rs.get = rs := List.ofFn_get rs
  have hstalk : stalkIdeal m.ker (m.base z) hz = Ideal.span (Set.range rs.get) := by
    rw [stalkIdeal_ker_eq_ker_stalkMap m z hz, ← hspan, ← ofList_ofFn_eq_span_range, hget]
  have hregFn : IsRegular (W.presheaf.stalk (m.base z)) (List.ofFn rs.get) := by
    rw [hget]; exact hreg
  obtain ⟨U, hzU, r, g, hgen, hregU⟩ := exists_affineOpen_span_eq_ideal_isRegular
    m.ker (m.base z) hz rs.get hstalk hregFn
  refine ⟨U, hzU, r, g, ?_, hregU⟩
  exact isGeneratedByOn_definingIdealOfHom_of_ker_app_eq_span m U.2 g
    ((Scheme.Hom.ker_apply m U).symm.trans hgen)

/-- **The defining ideal sheaf of a closed immersion with regular stalk kernels is regular.**
If the target is locally Noetherian and the kernel of the map of local rings is generated by a
regular sequence at every point of the source, then the defining ideal sheaf of the closed
immersion is a regular ideal sheaf.

The support of the quotient is the image of the closed immersion, so the affine criterion of
Stacks tag 063G has to be checked only at the points of that image, where
`exists_affineOpen_isGeneratedByOn_isRegular` supplies the data. -/
private theorem isRegularIdealSheaf_definingIdealOfHom_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap
    {Z W : Scheme.{u}} (m : Z ⟶ W) [IsClosedImmersion m] [IsLocallyNoetherian W]
    (h : ∀ z : Z, ∃ rs : List (W.presheaf.stalk (m.base z)),
      IsRegular (W.presheaf.stalk (m.base z)) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (m.stalkMap z).hom) :
    IsRegularIdealSheaf W.toRingedSpace
      (_root_.Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.definingIdealOfHom m) := by
  refine (isRegularIdealSheaf_iff_exists_affine_generators W _).mpr fun x hx => ?_
  rw [definingIdealQuotient_support_eq_range m] at hx
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨U, hzU, r, g, hgen, hregU⟩ := exists_affineOpen_isGeneratedByOn_isRegular m z (h z)
  exact ⟨U, hzU, r, g, hgen, hregU.toIsWeaklyRegular⟩

end StalkKernel

section StalkCriterion

/-- **A regular immersion generates each of its stalk kernels by a regular sequence.**  If
`f : Z ⟶ X` is a regular immersion then for every `z : Z` the kernel of `O_{X, f z} ⟶ O_{Z, z}`
is generated by a regular sequence of `O_{X, f z}`. -/
theorem exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_of_isRegularImmersion {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion f] (hf : IsRegularImmersion f) (z : Z) :
    ∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)), IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)) rs ∧
      Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap z).hom := by
  refine (exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_iff f z).mpr ?_
  have hz : f.liftCoborder.base z ∈ idealQuotientSupport
      f.coborderRange.toScheme.toRingedSpace
      (_root_.Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.definingIdealOfHom f.liftCoborder) := by
    rw [definingIdealQuotient_support_eq_range f.liftCoborder]
    exact ⟨z, rfl⟩
  exact exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap f.liftCoborder hf z hz

/-- **An immersion with regular stalk kernels over a locally Noetherian scheme is regular.**  The
converse of `exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_of_isRegularImmersion`;  this is the regular case of
Stacks tag 063I read along an immersion, and the Noetherian hypothesis is what lets a regular
sequence in a local ring be spread out to an affine neighbourhood. -/
theorem isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ X)
    [IsImmersion f] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (h : ∀ z : Z, ∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)),
      IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap z).hom) :
    IsRegularImmersion f := by
  change IsRegularIdealSheaf _
    (_root_.Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.definingIdealOfHom f.liftCoborder)
  refine isRegularIdealSheaf_definingIdealOfHom_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap
    f.liftCoborder fun z => ?_
  exact (exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_iff f z).mp (h z)

/-- **The regular locus of an immersion.**  The set of points of the source at which the kernel
of the induced map of local rings is generated by a regular sequence. -/
def regularStalkLocus {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ X) : Set Z :=
  {z | ∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)), IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)) rs ∧
    Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap z).hom}

/-- Membership in the regular locus is the condition on the kernel of the map of local rings. -/
theorem mem_regularStalkLocus {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ X) (z : Z) :
    z ∈ regularStalkLocus f ↔ ∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)),
      IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (f.base z)) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (f.stalkMap z).hom :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **The regular locus of an immersion into a locally Noetherian scheme is open.**  A regular
sequence generating the kernel at one point spreads out to regular generators of the defining
ideal sheaf over an affine open neighbourhood of the image point, and those generators generate
the kernel at every point of the source lying over that open. -/
theorem isOpen_regularStalkLocus {Z X : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion f]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] : IsOpen (regularStalkLocus f) := by
  rw [isOpen_iff_forall_mem_open]
  intro z hz
  obtain ⟨U, hzU, r, g, hgen, hregU⟩ := exists_affineOpen_isGeneratedByOn_isRegular
    f.liftCoborder z ((exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_iff f z).mp hz)
  have hregSeq : IsRegularSequenceOn f.coborderRange.toScheme.toRingedSpace U.1 g :=
    (isRegularSequenceOn_iff_isWeaklyRegular f.coborderRange.toScheme U.1 U.2 g).mpr
      hregU.toIsWeaklyRegular
  refine ⟨(f.liftCoborder ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 : Z.Opens), fun z' hz' => ?_,
    (f.liftCoborder ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 : Z.Opens).isOpen, hzU⟩
  refine (exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_liftCoborder_iff f z').mpr ?_
  exact exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_of_generators f.liftCoborder z' U.1 hz' g
    hregSeq hgen

end StalkCriterion

section ProjectiveDimension

/-- **Finite projective dimension of a quotient pair from finite projective dimension of the
target of a surjection.**  Let `φ : A → B` and `ψ : B → C` be surjections of commutative rings.
If `C` has finite projective dimension as a `B`-module through `ψ`, then `A ⧸ ker (ψ ∘ φ)` has
finite projective dimension as an `A ⧸ ker φ`-module through the induced map of quotients.

The first isomorphism theorem identifies `A ⧸ ker φ` with `B` and `A ⧸ ker (ψ ∘ φ)` with `C`, and
the square relating the two identifications to `ψ` and to the map of quotients commutes because
both quotient maps are induced from `A`.  Projective dimension is moved across the isomorphism of
base rings by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect.hasProjectiveDimensionLE_restrictScalars_ringEquiv` and then across
the resulting isomorphism of modules. -/
private theorem exists_hasProjectiveDimensionLT_quotient_of_surjective {A B C : Type u}
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C] (φ : A →+* B) (ψ : B →+* C)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ)
    (h : ∃ n : ℕ,
      let _ : Algebra B C := ψ.toAlgebra
      HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of B C) n) :
    ∃ n : ℕ,
      let _ : Algebra (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) (A ⧸ RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ)) :=
        (Ideal.Quotient.factor (Koszul.ker_le_ker_comp φ ψ)).toAlgebra
      HasProjectiveDimensionLT
        (ModuleCat.of (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) (A ⧸ RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ))) n := by
  let _ : Algebra B C := ψ.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := h
  have hn' : HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of B C) n := hn
  have hψφ : Function.Surjective (ψ.comp φ) := hψ.comp hφ
  let eI : (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) ≃+* B := RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hφ
  let eJ : (A ⧸ RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ)) ≃+* C := RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hψφ
  let _ : Algebra (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) (A ⧸ RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ)) :=
    (Ideal.Quotient.factor (Koszul.ker_le_ker_comp φ ψ)).toAlgebra
  have hsq : ∀ c : A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ,
      ψ (eI c) = eJ (Ideal.Quotient.factor (Koszul.ker_le_ker_comp φ ψ) c) := by
    intro c
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective c
    rfl
  have hres := AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect.hasProjectiveDimensionLE_restrictScalars_ringEquiv
    eI n (ModuleCat.of B C)
  let _ : Module (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) C :=
    ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} (eI : (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) →+* B)).obj
      (ModuleCat.of B C)).isModule
  have hres' : HasProjectiveDimensionLE (ModuleCat.of (A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) C) n := hres
  have hsmul : ∀ (c : A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ) (y : C), (c • y : C) = ψ (eI c) * y := fun _ _ => rfl
  let lin : C ≃ₗ[A ⧸ RingHom.ker φ] (A ⧸ RingHom.ker (ψ.comp φ)) :=
    { toFun := fun y => eJ.symm y
      map_add' := fun x y => map_add eJ.symm x y
      map_smul' := fun c y => by
        simp only [RingHom.id_apply]
        rw [hsmul c y, hsq c, map_mul, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply, Algebra.smul_def,
          RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]
      invFun := fun w => eJ w
      left_inv := eJ.apply_symm_apply
      right_inv := eJ.symm_apply_apply }
  exact ⟨n + 1, hasProjectiveDimensionLT_of_iso lin.toModuleIso (n + 1)⟩

/-- **The cotangent map of Stacks tag 09PV is injective for a perfect factor.**  For immersions
`i : Z ⟶ Y` and `j : Y ⟶ X` with `X` locally Noetherian and `i` perfect, the map
`I/𝔪I ⟶ J/𝔪J` induced by the inclusion of the kernel `I` of `O_{X, j (i z)} ⟶ O_{Y, i z}` in the
kernel `J` of `O_{X, j (i z)} ⟶ O_{Z, z}` is injective.

Perfectness of `i` gives finite projective dimension of `O_{Z, z}` over `O_{Y, i z}`, which
`exists_hasProjectiveDimensionLT_quotient_of_surjective` rewrites as finite projective dimension
of `A ⧸ J` over `A ⧸ I`;  that is the hypothesis of Stacks tag 09PV. -/
private theorem injective_mapQ_ker_stalkMap_of_perfect {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y)
    (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] [IsImmersion j] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect i] (z : Z) :
    Function.Injective
      ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom))).mapQ
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) •
          (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z)))
            (RingHom.ker ((i.stalkMap z).hom.comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom))))
        (Submodule.inclusion
          (Koszul.ker_le_ker_comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom (i.stalkMap z).hom))
        (Submodule.smul_top_le_comap_smul_top _ _)) := by
  have hY : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian j
  refine StacksDraft.Rodicio.injective_mapQ_maximalIdeal_of_finite_projectiveDimension
    (RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom)
    (RingHom.ker ((i.stalkMap z).hom.comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom))
    (RingHom.ker_ne_top _) (RingHom.ker_ne_top _)
    (Koszul.ker_le_ker_comp (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom (i.stalkMap z).hom) ?_
  refine exists_hasProjectiveDimensionLT_quotient_of_surjective
    (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom (i.stalkMap z).hom (j.stalkMap_surjective (i.base z))
    (i.stalkMap_surjective z) ?_
  let _ : Algebra (Y.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) (Z.presheaf.stalk z) :=
    (i.stalkMap z).hom.toAlgebra
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect.exists_hasProjectiveDimensionLE_stalk_of_perfect i z

end ProjectiveDimension

section Main

variable {Z Y X : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Y) (j : Y ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] [IsImmersion j]
  [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect i]

/-- **The local-ring conclusions of Stacks tag 09RK.**  If `i ≫ j` is a regular immersion and `i`
is perfect, then at every `z : Z` both the kernel of `O_{X, j (i z)} ⟶ O_{Y, i z}` and the kernel
of `O_{Y, i z} ⟶ O_{Z, z}` are generated by regular sequences. -/
private theorem exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_factors_of_perfect
    (hji : IsRegularImmersion (i ≫ j)) (z : Z) :
    (∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))),
        IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk (j.base (i.base z))) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (j.stalkMap (i.base z)).hom) ∧
      ∃ rs : List (Y.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)),
        IsRegular (Y.presheaf.stalk (i.base z)) rs ∧
          Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker (i.stalkMap z).hom :=
  exists_isRegular_generating_ker_stalkMap_factors i j z
    (injective_mapQ_ker_stalkMap_of_perfect i j z)
    (exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_of_isRegularImmersion (i ≫ j) hji z)

/-- **Stacks tag 09RK for the inner factor.**  Let `i : Z ⟶ Y` and `j : Y ⟶ X` be immersions of
schemes with `X` locally Noetherian and `i` perfect.  If the composite `i ≫ j` is a regular
immersion, then `i` is a regular immersion. -/
@[stacks 09RK "i is a regular immersion"]
theorem isRegularImmersion_of_perfect (hji : IsRegularImmersion (i ≫ j)) :
    IsRegularImmersion i := by
  have hY : IsLocallyNoetherian Y := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian j
  exact isRegularImmersion_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap i fun z =>
    (exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_factors_of_perfect i j hji z).2

/-- **Stacks tag 09RK for the outer factor, corrected statement (a Stacks erratum).**  Under the
same hypotheses there is an open `V ⊆ Y` containing the image of `i` such that the immersion
`V.ι ≫ j` of that open subscheme into `X` is regular.

The source concludes instead that `j` itself is a regular immersion, and that is false.  Over a
field `k`, take `Z = Spec k`, `Y = Spec k ⊔ Spec k`, `X = Spec k ⊔ Spec k[ε]/(ε²)`, let `i` be
the inclusion of the first component of `Y`, and let `j` be the identity on the first component
and the reduced point `Spec k ↪ Spec k[ε]/(ε²)` on the second.  All three hypotheses hold: `X` is
the spectrum of the Noetherian ring `k × k[ε]/(ε²)`, and `i` and `i ≫ j` are inclusions of a
component, hence open immersions, hence regular immersions, so `i` is perfect.  Yet `j` is not a
regular immersion: on the second component its ideal is `(ε) ⊆ k[ε]/(ε²)`, and no weakly regular
sequence generates it, since every element of `(ε)` kills `ε ≠ 0`.  This is
`Stacks.Examples.not_forall_isRegularImmersion_of_perfect_of_isRegularImmersion_comp`.

The hypotheses control `j` at the points of `i(Z)` and nowhere else — in the example `i(Z)` is
the first component, where `j` is an isomorphism — and the neighbourhood statement below is
exactly what the source's own local-ring argument supplies.  See also the implementation notes
of this file. -/
@[stacks 09RK "corrected statement (erratum): j is a regular immersion on an open neighbourhood \
of i(Z); the source's claim that j itself is a regular immersion is false"]
theorem exists_opens_isRegularImmersion_comp_of_perfect (hji : IsRegularImmersion (i ≫ j)) :
    ∃ V : Y.Opens, (∀ z : Z, i.base z ∈ V) ∧ IsRegularImmersion (V.ι ≫ j) := by
  refine ⟨⟨regularStalkLocus j, isOpen_regularStalkLocus j⟩,
    fun z => (exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_factors_of_perfect i j hji z).1, ?_⟩
  set V : Y.Opens := ⟨regularStalkLocus j, isOpen_regularStalkLocus j⟩
  obtain ⟨W, b, j', _, H, hj'⟩ := exists_open_isPullback_liftCoborder j V
  have hclosed : IsClosedImmersion j' := MorphismProperty.of_isPullback H.flip inferInstance
  refine (isRegularImmersion_iff_of_open (V.ι ≫ j) W j' hj').mpr ?_
  refine isRegularIdealSheaf_definingIdealOfHom_of_exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap j' fun v => ?_
  have h1 : ∃ rs : List (X.presheaf.stalk ((V.ι ≫ j).base v)),
      IsRegular (X.presheaf.stalk ((V.ι ≫ j).base v)) rs ∧
        Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker ((V.ι ≫ j).stalkMap v).hom := by
    rw [ker_stalkMap_isOpenImmersion_comp V.ι j v]
    exact v.2
  rw [← hj'] at h1
  exact (exists_isRegular_ker_stalkMap_comp_isOpenImmersion_iff j' W.ι v).mp h1

end Main

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

